C - LOOPS
==========

Repeat code multiple times.


FOR LOOP
--------
for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
    printf("Number: %d\n", i);
}

Syntax:
for (init; condition; increment) { ... }


WHILE LOOP
----------
int i = 0;
while (i < 10) {
    printf("%d\n", i);
    i++;
}

Continues while condition is true.


DO-WHILE
--------
int i = 0;
do {
    printf("%d\n", i);
    i++;
} while (i < 10);

Runs at least once.


BREAK & CONTINUE
-----------------
break;      Exit loop immediately
continue;   Skip to next iteration


COMMON USES
-----------
Iterate through array
Count numbers
Menu loops
Game loops


EXAMPLES
--------
Sum 1 to 10:
int sum = 0;
for (int i = 1; i <= 10; i++)
    sum += i;

Infinite loop (careful!):
while (1) { ... }


COMMON ERRORS
-------------
Infinite loops → Program hangs
Off-by-one → Wrong count
Forgot increment → Never exits


TIPS
----
Initialize before loop.
Check condition carefully.
Increment inside loop.
Test with small numbers first.
